Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:35:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/33] Updates from the Clicktrough fork

This build's update check reads the fork's manifest, which its release
workflow writes for each release of the meter rebuilt with the fork's
patches: the official package would replace them. A newer build of the
same version (its revision) is an update too, and the update window and
Settings name it.

Meter 2.0.80 fetches the manifest itself (update_check.rs) from a fixed
address, checks it with the original's signing key and installs only
packages from cdn.a2tools.app. Here the address is the fork's latest
release, only its packages are installed (not the original's CDN), and
its manifest, which that key
would refuse, is taken unsigned: over HTTPS from the fork's own releases,
with each package's SHA-256.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RahWACwaxzLAcYgwc9jk8C
